From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 10:23:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] RISC OS: flush before pushing the texture matrix for text

On the skirmish setup screen most option buttons and the map preview
were missing (a button appeared only while the pointer was over it).
The game made exactly the same GL calls as on a hardware driver; Mesa's
classic software renderer, which OSMesa uses, drew them differently.

Mesa's push_matrix() doesn't flush buffered immediate-mode vertices, and
pushing the texture matrix can reallocate its stack. Quads still in the
vertex buffer were then drawn with a wrong texture matrix, their texture
coordinates (0-256, scaled by the matrix) fell outside the texture, and
GL_CLAMP gave transparent texels. A 40-line GL program shows it on plain
Mesa 20.3.5 swrast; llvmpipe is fine, and so is swrast with
FLUSH_VERTICES() in push_matrix() (handed to riscos-mesa).

The game pushes the texture matrix in one place, before drawing text, so
a glFlush() there fixes it. No measurable cost (51 fps either way in
CAM_1A on the profiling host).
---
 lib/ivis_opengl/textdraw.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/ivis_opengl/textdraw.c b/lib/ivis_opengl/textdraw.c
index f710c57..f8e0f0f 100644
--- a/lib/ivis_opengl/textdraw.c
+++ b/lib/ivis_opengl/textdraw.c
@@ -631,6 +631,13 @@ void iV_DrawTextRotated(const char* string, float XPos, float YPos, float rotati
 	pie_SetTexturePage(TEXPAGE_FONT);
 
 	glGetIntegerv(GL_MATRIX_MODE, &matrix_mode);
+#if defined(WZ_OS_RISCOS)
+	// Mesa's classic software renderer (OSMesa) doesn't flush buffered
+	// vertices before glPushMatrix(), and pushing the texture matrix can
+	// move it: 2D images drawn just before some text then came out
+	// transparent (skirmish setup buttons, the map preview). Draw them now.
+	glFlush();
+#endif
 	glMatrixMode(GL_TEXTURE);
 	glPushMatrix();
 	glLoadIdentity();
